---
globs:
  - "site/**"
  - "package.json"
  - ".npmrc"
  - "package-lock.json"
  - "scripts/check-production-dependency-graph.mjs"
---

`site/` is workspace `pr-agent-landing`. Vercel installs from the root with `npm ci --workspace=pr-agent-landing --include-workspace-root=false` and builds with `npm run --workspace=pr-agent-landing build`. One root lockfile and `.npmrc` own install policy. `check:prod-deps` installs a clean backend production tree and queries installed packages. It rejects frontend-only packages and `express`, `hono`, `next`, `react`, or `vite` under `evlog`. React, Vite, and TanStack stay in `site/package.json`; the root keeps `site` under `workspaces` and adds no frontend dependency. `src/` never imports `site/`, and `site/lib/` never imports `src/`. Agent-facing copy stays in `site/lib/llmsKnowledge.ts`; `site/lib/content.ts` owns shared human copy. `site/public/llms.txt` must equal `renderLlmsTxt()`. `lint:backend` ignores `site/`; `test/settingsInventory.test.ts` checks root lock declarations for every workspace.
